Hello neighbours, here is the autumn newsletter from the residents' group.

The weather has finally turned. We lit the fire for the first time this seaso=
n last night, and the cat has claimed the rug in front of it as her own.

The neighbours' son has been practising the trumpet. He is improving, slowly,=
 and I have started to recognise the tune, which I think is meant to be a car=
ol.

Dad has been busy in his workshop building a bird table. It is a little lopsi=
ded, but the robins do not seem to mind, and he watches them from the kitchen=
 every morning.

We are thinking of a short trip to the coast next month. Nothing fancy, just =
a couple of nights somewhere quiet with a good walk and a decent place for fi=
sh and chips.

The swimming lessons are going well. Our youngest can now manage a length wit=
hout the float, and she is very proud of the certificate she brought home.

We had a power cut on Tuesday evening and ended up playing cards by candlelig=
ht. It was rather fun, though the children were less keen once they realised =
the internet was off.

Our holiday photos are finally sorted into albums. It brought back lovely mem=
ories, and we laughed at the one of you trying to put up the tent in the wind.

The choir concert went well. We were nervous about the new piece, but it came=
 together on the night, and the church was nearly full, which was lovely to s=
ee.

The book you lent me was wonderful. I stayed up far too late finishing it, an=
d I keep thinking about the ending; we should talk about it next time we meet.

I finally got round to framing the map you gave us. It is hanging in the hall=
 now, and visitors always stop to look for the places they know.

The repairs to the roof are done at last. The builders were tidy and quick on=
ce they started, and we no longer need the bucket in the attic when it rains.

We finally finished painting the spare room. It took far longer than planned,=
 mostly because we changed our minds about the colour twice, but it looks muc=
h brighter now.

See you at the next meeting, and thank you to everyone who helped this season.

--=20
Elm Street Residents' Group

